From {{inh|mi|poz-pol-pro|*puku₁}} (compare with {{cog|haw|puʻu}} and {{cog|ty|puʻu}}),<ref>{{cite-book|pages=371-2|title=Maori-Polynesian Comparative Dictionary|first= Edward|last=Tregear|year=1891|publisher=Lyon and Blair |location=Wellington, New Zealand|url=https://nzetc.victoria.ac.nz/tm/scholarly/tei-TreMaor-c1-10.html}}</ref><ref name=P/> from {{inh|haw|poz-oce-pro|*buku}} from {{inh|mi|poz-pro|*bukuh|id=joint, knuckle}} (compare with {{cog|ms|buku|t=node, lump, loaf}}).<ref name=P>{{R:Pollex|puku.1a}}</ref><ref>{{cite-book |page=175 | first = Malcolm D.  | last = Ross | first2=Andrew |last2= Pawley |first3=Meredith |last3=Osmond | year=  2016 | title = The lexicon of Proto-Oceanic | volume = 5: People, body and mind | location = Canberra | publisher = Australian National University | isbn = 9781922185327 }}</ref> Sense of stomach displaced {{m|mi|manawa}}. Also {{doublet|nocap=1|mi|kupu}}, see there for more details.

